Bead A SHIPPED in b743d7f0. My escalation that the approach was repo-forbidden
was too strong and was acted on. The guard forbids bare bd because it resolves
from $PWD; `bd -C "$RIG_ROOT" --readonly` pins the rig checkout and fails closed,
and the implementation extended the policy with its own triple-locked exemption
plus a regression test proving the exemption is narrow (4 passed at HEAD).

Also records: Bead B -> gcp-jkd3 (parked, rig drained, before/after measurement
confounded), Bead C -> gcp-7fgg, direction 2 -> gcp-d9uj; and that §9's pin
caveat expired (pin moved to fdfbedd7, reaper 1866 lines).

Direction 2's blocking constraint was overstated: a formula step CAN name a
content-hashed pack asset, and this repo already does it three times including
270 lines below the comment saying it cannot. gcp-d9uj reuses that pattern.

Third instance in this bead family of a stated blocker already solved elsewhere
in the tree. Check for shipped machinery before specifying new machinery.

